    "aiCategories": [],
    "aiDescription": "### General Description\nPerforms automated triage and investigation of Google SIEM alerts using AI agents. This action identifies if an alert originated from the Google SIEM detection engine and either retrieves an existing investigation or triggers a new one. It is an asynchronous action that polls for the investigation's completion to provide a final verdict, confidence score, and detailed summaries.\n\n### Flow Description\n1. Validates if the current alert originated from Google's SIEM detection engine by checking for a `SiemAlertId` in the alert's additional properties.\n2. On the first run, searches for any existing investigations associated with the alert ID via a GET request to the Google SecOps API.\n3. If no existing investigation is found, triggers a new investigation via a POST request to the Google SecOps API.\n4. Stores the investigation name in the alert context for tracking across polling cycles.\n5. In subsequent runs, retrieves the investigation name from the context and checks its status via a GET request.\n6. Once the investigation completes successfully, retrieves the verdict, confidence level, and detailed summaries.\n7. Formats the findings into Markdown reports (Alert Summary, Investigation Summary, Suggested Next Steps) and populates the action's JSON results.\n\n### Additional Notes\n* This action is asynchronous and will poll the Google SecOps API until the investigation reaches a terminal state.\n* The action requires the alert to have a `SiemAlertId` in its additional properties to execute.",
    "aiShortDescription": "Performs automated triage and investigation of Google SIEM alerts by triggering or retrieving an AI-driven investigation and polling for its final verdict, confidence score, and summary.",
    "parametersDescription": "There are no parameters for this action.",
